      "explanation": "The case contract defines HO1 as making the plan executable despite real‑world barriers (cost, transport, work, caregiver availability). While the doctor gave some transport and medication guidance, no targeted action beyond generic safety advice was taken to integrate these barriers into the plan; the ‘出院带药无’ confusion, family work/cost constraints, and need for caregiver coordination were not addressed with case‑specific executable alternatives.",
